# Imported audit evidence is stored byte-for-byte and its SHA-256 hashes are
# recorded in the MANIFEST.csv beside it. This repository is developed with
# core.autocrlf enabled, which rewrites line endings on checkout -- four of the
# imported artifacts are LF-only, so without this rule a fresh clone would hand
# back different bytes and every hash in the manifest would fail to verify.
#
# The point of importing originals is that a later reader can prove the bytes
# were not edited. Marking them -text is what makes that true on Windows too.
# Verified by tools/evidence/validate_csv_evidence.py.
core/audit/** -text

# P0.G4's type_snapshot.py hashes mobile/assets/data/equipment.json's raw
# bytes as sourceSha256 (canonical_json.file_sha256). Without a pinned eol,
# core.autocrlf=true (this repo's setting) checks this file out as CRLF on
# Windows and LF on a default Linux CI runner -- same content, two
# different hashes, which would fail test_generated_files_on_disk_match_a_
# fresh_build in CI for a reason that has nothing to do with the snapshot
# actually being stale. Pinning eol=lf makes every checkout produce the
# same bytes regardless of platform. Flagged in P0.G4's review round.
mobile/assets/data/equipment.json text eol=lf
core/equipment_identity/p0/*.json text eol=lf
